I'm a software developer with 13 years of commercial experience. I live in the Blue Mountains west of Sydney, so I'm mainly interested in remote opportunities.

My expertise is in functional programming, service-oriented cloud architectures, scalable data pipelines and data-engineering, and web development.

I spent most of 2020 working on my own startup in the digital identity space, which was an amazing experience, but made much harder by trying to do it during a global pandemic.

I'm passionate about the environment, privacy, civil liberties, and education. I'd ideally like to work for a company that's having a positive impact on the world.

For my next role I'm looking for something where I can step up and take on more responsibility. In particular, a role where I can work across both software development and product management would be ideal.

At university I focused on large scale parallel and distributed systems; various machine learning, data mining and AI techniques; and a healthy dose of pure theory and mathematics.
